+# The Daily Grind: field INP monitoring
+
+The homepage loads the self-hosted `assets/inp.js` module, built from `src/inp.js`
+with Google's `web-vitals/attribution`. No third-party runtime CDN is required.
+Run `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile`, `pnpm test`, and `pnpm build` after changes.
+The generated bundle is committed so the existing static hosting setup works
+without a build step. Deploy `index.html` and `assets/` together.
+
+## Collector configuration
+
+The `inp-endpoint` meta tag in `index.html` defaults to `/analytics/inp`.
+**This repository has no backend.** Configure your hosting platform to route
+`POST /analytics/inp` to your analytics ingestion service, or change the meta tag
+to an existing collector URL. That collector must accept JSON POST bodies,
+persist them, and return a successful status (for example, 204). An external
+collector also needs to allow the site's origin with CORS and be permitted by
+the site's CSP `connect-src`. An empty endpoint disables monitoring.
+
+Reports are deferred using `fetchLater` where available; the compatibility layer
+sends on document hidden with `sendBeacon`, then keepalive fetch if the beacon
+queue declines. Native deferred-request quota errors also use that fallback.
+Delivery is best effort; there is no response-dependent retry or local storage.
+No `unload`/`beforeunload` handlers or polling are installed.
+
+## Reading reports
+
+All durations and timestamps are milliseconds. Each report is a current INP
+snapshot, with `id`, `value`, `delta`, `rating`, and `navigationType`. Reports
+cover good and slow visits so the collector can calculate population p75.
+Upsert by metric `id` using the highest `sequence` (to handle out-of-order
+delivery); do not sum `value` or
+average the callbacks. Pending snapshots for the same ID are replaced before
+delivery, so `delta` alone is not suitable for aggregation. Back/forward cache
+restores receive distinct IDs from web-vitals. No report means no measurable
+interaction or an unsupported browser, not a zero INP score.
+
+- `inputDelay`, `processingDuration`, and `presentationDelay` separate main-thread
+  blocking before handlers, handler processing, and waiting for the next paint.
+- `interactionTarget` uses authored `data-inp-target` labels to identify homepage
+  links, falling back to a tag name. No text, form values, or page query strings
+  are collected.
+- `longestScript` identifies the biggest overlapping script, including its URL,
+  function, character position, invoker type, overlap duration, and INP `subpart`.
+  `scripts` contains up to five overlapping script entries sorted by overlap;
+  `scriptCount` indicates when the list was truncated. URLs omit credentials,
+  queries, and fragments. Raw performance entries and DOM nodes are never sent.
+- `forcedStyleDuration` and `forcedLayoutDuration` describe synchronous work
+  inside a script. Older implementations expose only the combined
+  `forcedStyleAndLayoutDuration` fallback.
+- `renderStyleDuration` and `renderLayoutDuration` sum frame rendering work
+  across the interaction's Long Animation Frames. They describe whole frames,
+  which may extend beyond the interaction. `totalStyleAndLayoutDuration` is the
+  library's combined attribution, including forced work; it is a fallback,
+  not another duration to add to those fields. `totalScriptDuration`,
+  `totalPaintDuration`, and `totalUnattributedDuration` provide further context.
+
+INP selection, interaction grouping, lifecycle reporting, and bfcache handling
+are delegated to web-vitals. `reportAllChanges` tracks updates throughout the
+visit; it does not report every slow interaction. Event Timing is required;
+unsupported browsers skip monitoring. Long Animation Frames are optional:
+basic INP reporting still works without them. Missing timing fields are `null`,
+distinct from measured zero, and `longAnimationFramesSupported` distinguishes
+an unsupported API from a visit with no matching long frame. LoAF attribution
+only includes long frames (over 50 ms) and eligible scripts (over 5 ms); browser
+security restrictions can also limit attribution. Treat it as diagnostic
+evidence rather than a complete performance trace.
+
+References: [web-vitals](https://github.com/GoogleChrome/web-vitals) and
+[Identify INP causes](https://developer.chrome.com/docs/modern-web-guidance/guides/performance/identify-inp-causes).
